From 7853058d5e7878ce3279618b8a58a121cd2834f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:23:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVDInputStreamNavigator: closing a disc never waits for the
 scan of its titles

CDiscSoftTelecineScan::Stop() joined the thread that reads the titles of the
disc, from the destructor, from the Close() of the player's navigator. A read
of a disc image on a share of the network that stopped answering kept the
stop of the video waiting until that read gave up.

The results of the scan are now shared by the thread and the navigator
(KODI::DISC::CScanResults); the thread owns what it reads with and runs
detached (RunDetached()). Stop() tells it to stop and returns at once; the
reads of the image fail from then on, the thread ends on its own when the read
it is in returns, and it touches nothing of the closed navigator; what it
found after the stop is neither told nor logged.

The titles are read one after the other, never several at once, and not at
all for a disc in a drive, as before, nor now for an image or a folder on an
optical disc (a device of the SCSI CD-ROM driver, major 11): a second reader
moves the head of the drive against the player's, and reading the titles
before the playing would keep it waiting seconds.

t_scanlife (built with the address and undefined behaviour sanitizers): with a
read that hangs 1.5 s, Stop() returns in under 1 ms and the stopped results
keep nobody waiting; the thread ends on its own, keeps the results while it
runs and lets them go; a title that is not planned is not waited for, one being
read is. A Stop() that waits for the thread takes 1.4 s and fails it.
